# Usually you do NOT need this.
#
# In production, netlify.toml proxies /api/* to the Render API, so the app's
# default relative /api works with no configuration and no CORS.
# In development, Vite proxies /api to localhost:4000 (see vite.config.ts).
#
# Only set this if you are hosting the frontend somewhere without that proxy,
# in which case it must be the full API origin with no trailing slash — and the
# API's CORS_ORIGIN must then list this site's URL.
# VITE_API_URL=https://chai-aged-accounts-api.onrender.com
